nstall -U black`\n41\t2. Use the online formatter at <https://black.vercel.app/?version=main>, which will use\n42\t   the latest main branch.\n43\t3. Or run _Black_ on your machine:\n44\t   - create a new virtualenv (make sure it's the same Python version);\n45\t   - clone this repository;\n46\t   - run `pip install -e .[d]`;\n47\t   - run `pip install -r test_requirements.txt`\n48\t   - make sure it's sane by running `python -m pytest`; and\n49\t   - run `black` like you did last time.\n50\t-->\n51\t\n52\t**Describe the bug**\n53\t\n54\t<!-- A clear and concise description of what the bug is. -->\n55\t\n56\t**To Reproduce**\n57\t\n58\t<!--\n59\tMinimal steps to reproduce the behavior with source code and Black's configuration.\n60\t-->\n61\t\n62\tFor example, take this code:\n63\t\n64\t```python\n65\t[\n66\t    (1, 2),\n67\t    # # fmt: off\n68\t    # (3,\n69\t    #    4),\n70\t    # # fmt: on\n71\t    (5, 6),\n72\t]\n73\t```\n74\t\n75\tAnd run it with these arguments:\n76\t\n77\t```sh\n78\t$ black file.py\n79\t```\n80\t\n81\tThe resulting error is:\n82\t\n83\t> error: cannot format file.py: INTERNAL ERROR: Black 25.11.0 on Python (CPython) 3.11.13 produced different code on th\n84\t~~~~\n85\t\n86\t### candidate #10 (score 0.11, open, labels ['S: needs repro', 'T: bug'])\n87\ttitle: INTERNAL ERROR code that is not equivalent to the source (non-UTF8, iso-8859-1)\n88\t\n89\t~~~~ untrusted\n90\t**Describe the bug**\n91\t\n92\tHistoric behaviour:\n93\t\n94\t```\n95\t❯ black --version && black --diff tests/test_cases/not_utf8.py\n96\tblack, 23.9.1 (compiled: no)\n97\tPython (CPython) 3.13.5\n98\tAll done! ✨ 🍰 ✨\n99\t1 file would be left unchanged.\n100\t```\n101\t\n102\t```\n103\t❯ black --version && black --diff tests/test_cases/not_utf8.py\n104\tblack, 25.12.0 (compiled: no)\n105\tPython (CPython) 3.13.5\n106\tAll done! ✨ 🍰 ✨\n107\t1 file would be left unchanged.\n108\t```\n109\t\n110\tNew behaviour:\n111\t\n112\t```\n113\t❯ black --version && black --diff tests/test_